44	     * when blank (off); the entry date, null when blank (off); the grace days, null when blank (off); the pot, two decimals or null for none; the alert threshold, two decimals or null for off; the parent sheet's id, null for none; the fiscal start month, 1 to 12; the escalation gap in days, null when blank (off); the review SLA in days, null when blank (none); the pending SLA in days, null when blank (none); the maximum of open claims per person, null when blank (none); the proof kinds, comma separated, null when blank (none); the default grade, null when blank (A); the mid and high score thresholds, null when blank (none); the score log switch, "on" or null when blank (off); the retired grades, in the order retired; the sheet's grades, A, B and C then those added in the order added; the from-dates of the policy versions in the order
45	     * recorded (the current version is their count; null for none counts on every date); and every value recorded for the dated settings, from which the screen works out the one in
